findings.description:
`excluded_tests` is part of the case id (D9, line 227; 421 D1). When 424 calls `qualification_for(case, environment)` in a new environment and then `qualify_candidate`, one of three things happens:
- the candidate still qualifies with the same exclusions;
- it is rejected, which the design covers;
- it still qualifies but with a different flaky or failing-at-reference set.

In the third case the new record's `case_id` is not in the case set version 424 loaded. Line 242 covers only the rejection case. The record is keyed on commit, not case id, so the new record silently points at a case that is not in the set. Fix: define what 424 gets back here. Options: treat it as a drop with a named reason, as a substitution that 424 records, or as a requirement to write a new case set version. The architecture requires results to reference "the case and the set version it was run under", so this cannot stay implicit.

Every success criterion in the slice plan entry maps to a decision and a test:
- per-node hidden and superseded sets, including added `conftest.py` fixtures (D3);
- issue text frozen at the cutoff (D2);
- every candidate ends in a recorded outcome (D1, D10);
- repeats with an exclusion list that is part of case identity (D9);
- records keyed on environment identity, with re-qualification (D10);
- a yield report run on two projects (D12, walkthrough).

No scope assigned to 422 is dropped.
